Package: t2-bootloader
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: zhongfu <me@zhongfu.li>
Depends: util-linux
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: ZSpace T2 boot chain (U-Boot) and its offline updater
 Mainline U-Boot for the ZSpace T2 (Rockchip RK3568): the plain and installer
 boot-chain images (idbloader/u-boot .itb pairs) and their compiled default
 environments, plus /usr/sbin/t2-bootloader-install, which writes the SPL to
 LBA 0x40 and U-Boot to LBA 0x4000 of a target disk after validating both
 images and confirming the write.
 .
 The U-Boot environment (/uboot.env on the FAT boot partition) is never touched
 by the updater; it belongs to the running system, not to this package.  The
 files under /usr/lib/t2-bootloader are raw artefacts for the image build as
 well: the image repository consumes them to assemble the installer card.
